        "Treasured Tales of the Chouken Shinkageuchi is a one-volume Inazuma collection sold by Kuroda at Yae Publishing House. Its volume is also called Shinkageuchi and was once a restricted text. It presents itself as a traditional novel and tells a fantastical account of the twin sisters Makoto and Ei as the first Shogun and her kagemusha.",
        "The text introduces paired sword terms: Shinuchi are works offered to a lord or deity and kept pure, while Kageuchi are given to retainers as weapons and become bloodstained. This is the book’s symbolic framing of light and shadow, not a complete technical history of Inazuman sword schools."
