        "Ei’s own voice-over calls the account in Treasured Tales largely accurate. That endorsement gives the work unusual evidentiary weight, but its stated genre and Ei’s qualification still matter: it is a novel, and its portrayal of the sisters is an authored account rather than a neutral transcript."
